## Flight Report

**Left gate:** Crossed during the forward move at decision k=11 (from x≈2.37,y≈-0.30 to x≈3.11,y≈-0.78, heading ≈-25°). The downward panel showed the crossbar directly overhead with a post at the frame edge — the calibrated "in the opening" signature — and the following frame showed open room with no posts, confirming a clean transit. Line-up was messy (several turn-direction mistakes at k=3–k=7 cost most of the budget), but the actual crossing at k=11 followed the correct straight-through procedure.

**Center gate:** Never located. After the left-gate crossing I searched deeper into the room (k=12, k=13) but only found furniture, shelving, and a mannequin — no yellow/teal posts. Not crossed.

**Penguin:** Never located — no black-and-white shape on a low table appeared in any downward view after the left gate.

**Final pose:** x≈3.78, y≈-1.08, z≈1.52, heading ≈-30° (about to execute a final +20° left turn) when the flight ended at the 14-decision limit.

**Verdict:** Task not completed. Only the left gate was crossed (through the middle, per the calibrated signature); the center gate and the penguin hover were not achieved — the decision budget was consumed by recovering from lineup errors early in the left-gate approach.
